Description: Tell one trusted client which window is where, and show it one
 Adds zyantrik_window_locator_v1, a private protocol offered only to the one
 client labwc launches itself on a pre-connected socket from
 <yantrik locator="command"> (launch-client.c), and again as soon as it exits
 (at most every 5 s). The client may ask which window is at a point, which
 window has focus, and for a picture of the window it was last told about,
 rendered offscreen from that window's own scene subtree (scene-capture.c)
 and handed over in a sealed memory file. Every event answers a request, so
 the client learns about no window it did not ask about. A picture needs a
 fresh answer: only the window the most recent answer named, within 2 s, and
 once. At most 120 answers and 2 pictures a second; nothing is answered
 while the session is locked. The point lookup looks through the client's
 own surfaces, so the overlay it draws during a drag does not hide the
 window under it.
 Built for Yantrik OS's Y Anywhere (design/y-anywhere-2026-11-22.md).
Author: Yantrik OS <dev@yantrikos.com>
Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-11-23
